---
description: Plain-writing rules for docs, READMEs, commit messages and PR text
globs: ["**/*.md", "**/*.mdx", "**/*.rst", "**/*.txt"]
alwaysApply: false
---

When you write or edit prose in this project:

1. Start with the answer or the fact. No `Certainly!` or warm-up lines.
2. Plain words: `use` (not `leverage` or `utilize`), `start` (not `embark`), `many` (not `a plethora of`).
3. No hype: no `blazing fast`, `seamless`, `game-changer`, `revolutionary`. Give numbers you measured, or say nothing.
4. No `It's not X, it's Y`. No em dashes. No emoji at the start of headings or list items.
5. Sentences under 25 words when you can.
6. Keep facts, commands, links and code exactly as they are.

Then reread what you wrote and fix anything that breaks these rules.
